---
globs: "*.vhd*"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Instantiation:
    - Output port maps cannot use aggregates in VHDL. Use dot notation instead.
    - Don't use record aggregates with single item. Use dot notation instead.

- Naming convention
    - AXI-Streaming port names should be m_axis_*/s_axis_*, or m_axis_<function_*>_*/s_axis_<function_*> if there is ambiguity between ports.
    - AXI-Streaming signals in modules should be named <function>_*. If a bidirectional bus pair is used (like BSB interface), signals can be prefixed m2s_<function>_* or s2m_<function>_* to distinguish the signal direction.

- Use VHDL2008 features:
    - All projects are in VHDL2008, so use VHDL2008 idioms whenever possible
    - Use when stamenents instead of short if blocks
    - Allow generics to depend on previous generics
    - use "if/else generate" instead of multiple exclusive "if generate" statements
    - use switch generates when appropriate
    - Take advantage of auto casting of std_logic to bool in conditional "if" and "when" statements (replace if x='1' to if x)
    
        -  Multi-term tests could also be simplified if all the elements are equality tests with std_logic. Don't mix std_logic and booleans in an expression, e.g. "(a='1' and b='0') and c>1" cannot be replaced by "(a and b) and c>1" because "(a and b)" is std_logic and "c>1" is boolean.   
    - All processes should now use process(all) (without sensitivity list)
    - Eliminate _int_ variable that are directly assigned to ports combinatorially. VHDL 2008 allows reading output ports.



- General VHDL rules

    - Prefer aggregate assignment for std_logic_vector when assigning multiple bits: ``v := (0 => x, 1 => y, others => '0')`` instead of individual ``v(i) := ...`` statements.
    - Each entity in a file *must* be preceded with the library it needs. This is because libraries are forgotten when the previous architecture definition ends.
    - Don't use metasignals such as Don't-care or Hizh-Z (``'-', 'Z'``): Those haveno meaning in synthesis.

- Vivado specific rules

    - Have only one "if rising_edge(...)" per process. Vivado simulator crashes otherwise.





- AXI-Streaming bus rules
    - Do not add unnecessary conditional assignment of TDATA or TVALID to set those signals when TVALID is low anyway.   


- Resets
    - Use synchronous resets
    - Put reset handling in its own ``if rst`` block at the **bottom** of the process (after the main case/if logic). That way reset overrides normal assignments and every branch of the main logic can assign all registers; this avoids creating latches.

- VHDL comment extraction (vhdl_sphinx_domain)

    - Comments blocks that end before elements (without a blank line), such as entity, architecture, signals etc.,  are comments attached to this element
    - Commment blocks are treated as RST format and can be imported automatically in the documentation 
    - Title underlines in comments must match title length exactly

    - The Sphinx directive .. autoentity:: imports the comment block before the directive, and creates a table of generics and ports.
    - Memory map tables:
        - Are comment block with a table in markdown format 
        - Tables are directly imported into the documentation. 
        - The first line of the comment block is a marker is used to identify the comment block to import. 
        - Table separators (dashed lines) before/after tables are OK; parser removes them
        - Blank lines within tables break parsing; avoid them
        - Memory map markers: "Memory Map" or "Memory map" (case sensitive in :start-after)
        - Do not start block comments with dashed lines (----); 
        - Add blank line after marker before table separator
        - Memory map tables include address ranges, bit fields, and descriptions. Here is the format:

            -- Memory Map
            --
            -- | Page | Addr | Bit(s)|     Name                | Description                           |
            -- |------|------|-------|-------------------------|---------------------------------------|
            -- | CONTROL | 0:3 | 31:0 | field_name | Description text |

